 contract/unreachable-cause/socket-dir-refused · instance-unreachable causes · socket-dir-refused — A refused socket directory is reported with the cause word socket-dir-refused, each cause its own code word.
@@ -909,2 +909,3 @@
 decision/proptest-for-randomized-data · proptest for randomized data — Randomized test data comes from proptest strategies, with seeds persisted in committed regression files.
+decision/screen-fixture-box-rows-as-literals · Box rows recorded as their literals alone — A recorded screen fixture keeps a box rule row as its rule chars alone and the box's prompt row under that rule as the prompt char alone, and the fixture hygiene walk refuses a prompt row with text after the prompt char or a rule row with any other text. · guard: planted_box_row_beyond_its_literal_is_rejected
 decision/socket-dir-check-leaves-dir-as-found · Socket-directory check never repairs — The socket-directory check never chmods the directory it checks; a refused socket directory is left as found.
@@ -1015,3 +1016,3 @@
 decision/no-cache-in-release-workflow · No build cache in a release workflow — The Rust build cache is used in ci.yml only, never in a release workflow.
-decision/no-ignored-advisories · No advisory ignored — cargo deny ignores no advisory. · guard: CI job supply-chain
+decision/no-ignored-advisories · No advisory ignored — cargo deny ignores no advisory. · guard: CI job supply-chain · except: An advisory that sits only in an rmcp feature banned or off in the release graph is ignored with a reason naming that feature, standing until rmcp leaves <3.5.
 decision/no-workflow-concurrency · No workflow concurrency block — No workflow has a concurrency block; zizmor's concurrency-limits finding is declined and stays visible. · why: A concurrency group cancels pending runs even without cancel-in-progress, which would drop a push's always() gate and upload chain.
